From 53ccea063251fbbc2c7249d095cda46df24de5f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yinxing Hou <yihou@crs-m2m-cpu-spur-012.us-east2-a.compute.internal>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 10:46:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/25] Add sglang DSA patch: fix HIP indexer top-k row
 mismatch under DP-attention

Enables DP-attention + EAGLE MTP to run together for GLM-5.2 DSA on gfx950.
Previously the combination crashed on the first batch with:

    RuntimeError: Expected lengths.size(0) == B to be true, but got false.

In dsa_indexer.py::_get_topk_paged the CUDA path slices its paged-MQA inputs to
the real (unpadded) row count q_offset, which is what `lengths` is sized to,
then restores the padding afterwards. The aiter/HIP path does neither: it sizes
its `logits` output from the DP-padded q_fp8.shape[0], and the padding-restore
was gated `not _is_hip`. Under DP-attention the hidden states are padded, so the
top-k saw score.shape[0] != lengths.shape[0] and asserted.

The patch makes HIP follow the CUDA contract. Both guards are false when no
padding is present, so the non-DP path is unchanged.

Not the same defect as sglang PR #30378/#30427, which fixed CUDA-side padded row
*values* (seqlens_expand_kernel clamp, already present); this fixes the HIP-side
row *count*.

Verified on 8x MI355X (gfx950), ROCm 7.2.0, sglang 0.5.15.post1, GLM-5.2-MXFP4,
single node dp8+ep8 + EAGLE steps=3: 4/4 correctness, accept length median
3.86/4 (n=251), conc=64 1k/1k 256/256 requests 0 failed, median TPOT 17.2 ms.
DP-attention-only and MTP-only regressions unchanged.

Known limitation: under PD disaggregation with MTP on the decode leg the crash
is gone and the server starts clean, but the first routed request deadlocks in
the EAGLE draft-extend metadata path -- a separate defect, not addressed here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
